# kin/child/legs/far: the FAR leg of the child's side walk (and the Play posture's hop), a whole leg on its own part (P2b
# rollout, KIN-CHILD, 2026-10-22; docs/MOTION_P2.md, STYLE_P2 10; the adult's legs/adult/loco/far is the model). The legs
# layer draws this part first (z -1) and kin/child/legs/std (the near leg) over it: the far leg is drawn whole, the
# child idle's 4 px leg (5 where it slants, the full thickness across the bone), and only what the near leg covers is
# hidden. Its value: the idle's far leg (cloth 1 3 2 1 over the near's 1 4 3 1; leather h g under the near's i h), never
# thinner. Side views only (R, L) of the walk keys and hop; the front and back views are empty (std draws both legs
# there). Written with std by the KIN-CHILD generator (the near and far legs of each key from one design); the boots are
# boots_child's one drawing, placed by `put` (a row of tilt by its columns, never squashed).
use person
body child
role legs std
layer legs
z -1
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_child
tags boots-stamped

view D key walkA origin 0 0
|.
regions
|.

view D key walkA2 origin 0 0
|.
regions
|.

view D key walkB2 origin 0 0
|.
regions
|.

view D key walkC origin 0 0
|.
